===============================================================================================================================
Converting between Binary and Hexademical:
    Going from 0x -> 0b:
        Since Hex uses 4 bits to represent a character, switch the character representations with their binary counterparts:
            0x451 ... 
                4 = 0x0100, 5 = 0x0101, 1 = 0x0001
            Then combine them ...
                0b010001010001
    Going from 0b -> 0x
        The reverse ...
            0b0100 - 0101 - 0001
            4 - 5 - 1
            0x451

==============================================================================================================================
A powers-less way of converting from decimal to binary
    Build a binary by checking parity with division
    Builds from right to left
    if decimal value is even, next bit is a 0
    if decimal value is odd, next bit is a 1

EXAMPLE:
    CONVERT 422
    422 is even, so d(0) is 0 = 0
    422 / 2 is 211, which is odd, so d(1) is 1 = 10
    211 / 2 is 105, which is odd, so d(2) is 1 = 110
    105 / 2 is 52, which is even, so d(3) is 0 = 0110
    52 / 2 is 26, which is even, so d(4) is 0 = 00110
    26 / 2 is 13, which is odd, so d(5) is 1 = 100110
    13 / 2 is 6, which is even, so d(6) is 0 = 0100110
    6 / 2 is 3, which is odd, so d(7) is 1 = 10100110
    3 / 2 is 1, which is odd, so d(8) is 1 = 110100110
    1 / 2 is 0, so any digit above will be 0, so the algorithm terminates

SO:
    0d422 = 0b110100110

